# UARoute

Ukrainian-language **route atlas** (Ukraine → Europe). Brand: **UARoute** / uaroute.com. Stack: Next.js App Router + Tailwind v4, static export to S3.

## Do

- Keep user-visible strings in Ukrainian.
- Put catalog facts in `src/data/` (`types.ts`, `cities.ts`, `routes.ts`, `carriers.ts`).
- Put inquiry logic in `src/lib/whatsapp.ts` and events in `src/lib/analytics.ts`.
- Use existing editorial utilities (`type-display`, `container-page`, `rule-strong`) before adding CSS.
- After UI changes, verify in the browser and check view-source on a route page for the H1.

## Don't

- Don't invent timetables, prices, ratings, durations or availability.
- Don't add Lovable (`@lovable.dev`, `__lovableEvents`) or a shadcn `components/ui` dump.
- Don't restyle or extend `legacy/` (Create React App) unless asked.
- Don't send phone numbers or names through `track()`.

## Deploy

`npm run build` writes `./out`. `make deploy` uploads that directory to `s3://uaroute.com`. True request-time SSR needs a later host change; keep modules server-safe either way.
